{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>That you may know that I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> From here — from 'and I led you [uprightly]' — until the end of the passage, these are the words of HaShem; Moses did not say them. As our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Parashat Ki Tissa regarding 'and all the earth which I said' — it should say 'which you said'! Rather, up to here are the words of the disciple; from here onward are the words of the Master."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:40.290910646Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}